### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### 10 - MEMORY, COMPACTION & LONG-TERM CONTEXT SEARCH
###
### Amsha Agent uses a dual-SQLite memory system:
###
###   amsha-meta.db (primary WAL)
###     └─ chat_memory            - rolling LangChain4J chat window (max 100 msgs)
###     └─ compaction_summary     - summaries from ContextCompactionService runs
###     └─ agent_checkpoint       - per-session ReAct state
###     └─ rag_chunk              - RAG document chunks (Phase 64-C3+)
###     └─ session_registry       - (channelType, channelId, userId) → sessionId (Phase 64-B3+)
###
###   amsha-fts.db (FTS5)
###     └─ compaction_summary_fts - full-text indexed summaries, queryable via MemorySearchTool
###
### SystemMessage objects are NEVER stored in chat_memory (Nuance #1).
### Only UserMessage and AiMessage entries are persisted.
###
### Compaction trigger:
###   When chat window exceeds: threshold (10 messages) OR max-chars (96000) OR max-tokens (32000)
###   → ContextCompactionService summarises the oldest messages via llama-3.1-8b-instant
###   → Summary stored in both meta.db (compaction_summary) and fts.db (FTS5 index)
###   → Most recent 5 messages kept verbatim in the rolling window
###   → Audit event: CONTEXT_COMPACTED
###
### Phase 64 changes affecting this file:
###   Phase 64-A fix A3: Non-ASCII queries no longer silently return empty.
###   Phase 64-A fix A6: Compaction inFlight lock is released after observer failure.
###   Phase 64-C3: RAG chunks stored in rag_chunk table, not "rag:" prefix in compaction_summary.
###   Phase 64-D1: Compaction summary truncation is now codepoint-safe (emoji/CJK safe).
###
### RecallMemorySearchTool (tool name: "recall_memory_search"):
###   Queries FTS5 using userId scope - tenant-isolated.
###   Available to: coordinator, researcher, architect, synthesizer.
###   Input: {query: "<search terms>"}
###   Returns: top-N matching compaction summaries (after Phase 64-C3: RAG not mixed in)
###
### ArchivalMemorySearchTool (tool name: "archival_memory_search"):
###   Queries archival knowledge base for stored facts/patterns.
###   Available to: coordinator, researcher, architect, synthesizer.
###   Input: {query: "<search terms>", type: "FACT"|"PATTERN"|"CODE"|null}
###   Returns: matching archival entries.
###
### Core memory blocks (user_profile, active_task, constraints):
###   Structured user memory stored as key-value blocks.
###   read_core_memory → reads all blocks or specific block.
###   core_memory_append, core_memory_replace → modify blocks.
###
### Conversation continuity:
###   Chat memory (ChatMemoryStore) is NOT wiped on session soft-reset (/reset).
###   Only the ReAct checkpoint state is cleared. LLM retains conversational context.
###
### Prerequisites: Amsha Agent serve mode, AMSHA_LLM_API_KEY set
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# @baseUrl  = http://localhost:8080
# @validKey = key-internal-cWevfEoRvstUv0PqGpf02LzDY5kPNaz1y9GSl0LZOwU=

# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# MULTI-TURN CONVERSATION
# The rolling chat memory makes the agent aware of prior exchanges
# within the same session. Tests conversational continuity.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [MEM-0] Create session for multi-turn test
# @name memSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### [MEM-1] First message - establish a fact
# NOTE: Amsha Agent is on Quarkus 3.27.2 (Phase 60.1 migration).
# Do NOT use 3.23.0 here - that is the pre-migration version.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Remember this: my project is called Amsha Agent and it uses Quarkus 3.27.2.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### [MEM-2] Second message - recall from chat memory (no tools needed)
# The LLM sees the prior turn in its rolling window (PersistentChatMemoryStore).
# Expect: agent replies with "Amsha Agent" and "Quarkus 3.27.2"
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What was the project name I told you about, and which framework does it use?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}


###

GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/status/coordinator
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}


###


POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run-async
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/approve",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}


###

### [MEM-3] Third turn - build on the context
# Amsha Agent uses Quarkus 3.27.2 (LTS, released 2025).
# Quarkus 3.27.2 requires JDK 17+ (or 21+ for Virtual Threads) minimum;
# Amsha Agent itself uses JDK 25 (as per mise.toml: java = "temurin-25").
# Expect: agent recalls Quarkus 3.27.2 and can discuss its JVM requirements.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "Given what you know about my project, what JVM version does Quarkus 3.27.2 require?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 2
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{memSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SOFT RESET - CHAT MEMORY PRESERVED
# /reset clears ReAct checkpoint state, NOT the chat window.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [MEM-RESET-0] Create session
# @name resetMemSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### Establish a fact
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{resetMemSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "My favourite language is Kotlin.",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### Soft reset - wipes checkpoint, preserves chat memory
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{resetMemSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "/reset",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

### Recall after reset - must still know the fact
# Expect: agent responds with "Kotlin" (from the preserved chat window)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{resetMemSession.response.body.sessionId}}/run
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

{
    "goal": "What is my favourite programming language?",
    "agentRole": "coordinator",
    "maxIterations": 1
}

###

DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions/{{resetMemSession.response.body.sessionId}}
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###


# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# ROLLING WINDOW PRUNING
# Chat window max: 100 messages (amsha.chat-memory.max-messages).
# Compaction threshold: 10 messages (amsha.memory.compaction.threshold).
# Keep-recent: 5 messages preserved verbatim after compaction.
# Send 12+ sequential messages to trigger compaction.
# Watch logs for: [CompactionService] compaction triggered session=...
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### [MEM-4] Create dedicated session for window pruning test
# @name pruneSession
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/sessions
Content-Type: application/json
X-Amsha-API-Key: {{validKey}}

###

### Msgs 1–22: each is one turn in the rolling window.
### Around msg 15, compaction may trigger (watch logs).
### After msg 22, the oldest 2 are pruned from the active window.

